Apply mark-to-market election under IRC § 1296.
Mark-to-market election allows U.S. shareholder to include unrealized gains (and deduct unrealized losses, subject to limitation) annually, avoiding the harsh excess distribution regime and interest charge.
Requirements: - PFIC stock must be "marketable stock" (regularly traded on qualified exchange) - Election made on Form 8621 - Annual FMV must be determinable
Benefits: - No interest charge on deferred tax - Unrealized gains taxed as ordinary income annually - Unrealized losses deductible as ordinary loss (limited to prior years' gains) - Simple to calculate (no need for PFIC Annual Information Statement)
Reference: IRC § 1296, Form 8621 Part IV
Y Y Y
// Calculate unrealized gain/loss double fmv_change = pfic.mtm_fmv_year_end - pfic.mtm_fmv_year_start;
if (fmv_change > 0) { // Unrealized gain: include as ordinary income pfic.mtm_unrealized_gain = fmv_change; pfic.mtm_unrealized_loss = 0.0; pfic.mtm_ordinary_income = fmv_change; pfic.mtm_ordinary_loss = 0.0;
// Track cumulative gains for future loss limitation pfic.mtm_loss_limitation += fmv_change; } else if (fmv_change < 0) { // Unrealized loss: deductible as ordinary loss, limited to prior gains pfic.mtm_unrealized_loss = Math.abs(fmv_change); pfic.mtm_unrealized_gain = 0.0;
// Loss limited to cumulative prior gains if (pfic.mtm_unrealized_loss <= pfic.mtm_loss_limitation) { pfic.mtm_ordinary_loss = pfic.mtm_unrealized_loss; pfic.mtm_loss_limitation -= pfic.mtm_unrealized_loss; } else { pfic.mtm_ordinary_loss = pfic.mtm_loss_limitation; pfic.mtm_loss_limitation = 0.0; }
pfic.mtm_ordinary_income = 0.0; } else { // No change in FMV pfic.mtm_unrealized_gain = 0.0; pfic.mtm_unrealized_loss = 0.0; pfic.mtm_ordinary_income = 0.0; pfic.mtm_ordinary_loss = 0.0; }
// Income from PFIC (net of gain/loss) pfic.income_from_pfic = pfic.mtm_ordinary_income - pfic.mtm_ordinary_loss;
// Tax on ordinary income (at 21% corporate rate) if (pfic.income_from_pfic > 0) { pfic.tax_liability_from_pfic = pfic.income_from_pfic * 0.21; } else { pfic.tax_liability_from_pfic = 0.0; }
Mark-to-Market Election (IRC § 1296).
Shareholder includes unrealized gains and losses annually based on year-end fair market value of PFIC stock.
Treatment: - Unrealized gains: Included as ordinary income (not capital gain) - Unrealized losses: Deductible as ordinary loss, limited to cumulative prior years' mark-to-market gains
Benefits: - Avoids excess distribution regime and interest charge - No need for PFIC Annual Information Statement (unlike QEF) - Simple calculation based on year-end FMV
Requirements: - PFIC stock must be "marketable stock" per IRC § 1296(e): * Regularly traded on qualified exchange, or * Regularly traded on national market system, or * Stock for which FMV is available on continuing basis - Election made on Form 8621, Part IV
Basis Adjustments: - Basis increased by mark-to-market gains - Basis decreased by mark-to-market losses
Loss Limitation: - Losses cannot exceed cumulative mark-to-market gains from prior years - Prevents double benefit (both mark-to-market loss and capital loss on sale)
Reference: IRC § 1296, Treas. Reg. § 1.1296-1, Form 8621 Part IV
Y Y N
// Mark-to-market election invalid for non-marketable stock // Fall back to excess distribution regime pfic.taxation_method = "excess_distribution"; pfic.mtm_ordinary_income = 0.0; pfic.mtm_ordinary_loss = 0.0; pfic.income_from_pfic = 0.0; pfic.tax_liability_from_pfic = 0.0;
Mark-to-Market Election Invalid - Stock Not Marketable.
Mark-to-market election under IRC § 1296 is only available for "marketable stock" (regularly traded on qualified exchange or national market system).
Private PFIC stock or stock traded on foreign exchanges not meeting the marketable stock definition cannot use mark-to-market election.
Shareholder should consider QEF election if PFIC provides annual information statement, or accept default excess distribution regime.
Reference: IRC § 1296(e), Treas. Reg. § 1.1296-2
