// Apply apportionment to federal taxable income apportionment.apportioned_income = result.taxable_income * apportionment.apportionment_percentage;
// Apply state-specific adjustments apportionment.state_taxable_income = apportionment.apportioned_income + apportionment.state_additions - apportionment.state_subtractions;
// Calculate state tax apportionment.state_tax = apportionment.state_taxable_income * apportionment.state_tax_rate;
// Subtract state credits apportionment.state_tax = Math.max(0.0, apportionment.state_tax - apportionment.state_credits);
// Calculate refund or amount owed apportionment.state_refund_or_owed = apportionment.state_payments - apportionment.state_tax;
State tax calculation:
1. Apportion federal taxable income: Apportioned income = Federal taxable income × Apportionment %
2. Apply state adjustments: State additions: Interest on federal bonds, IRC 199A deduction, etc. State subtractions: Municipal bond interest, state taxes, etc.
3. Calculate state taxable income: State TI = Apportioned income + Additions - Subtractions
4. Apply state tax rate: State tax = State TI × State rate
5. Subtract state credits
6. Compare to payments to determine refund/owed
Reference: State corporate income tax instructions
