// ======================================== // Schedule M-1 Line 2: Federal Tax per Books // ======================================== // Book accounting records federal tax expense // This is added back because federal tax is not deductible for federal tax result.m1_federal_tax_per_books = result.federal_tax;
// ======================================== // Schedule M-1 Line 3: Excess Capital Losses // ======================================== // Corporations can only deduct capital losses to extent of capital gains // Any excess is not deductible (carried back/forward) // Simplified: Assume no capital transactions for now result.m1_excess_capital_losses = 0.0;
// ======================================== // Schedule M-1 Line 4: Income Subject to Tax NOT Recorded on Books // ======================================== // Rare - prepaid income recognized for tax but deferred for books result.m1_income_not_on_books = 0.0;
// ======================================== // Schedule M-1 Line 5: Expenses Recorded on Books NOT Deducted // ======================================== double expenses_not_deducted = 0.0;
// 50% of meals and entertainment (only 50% deductible for tax) // Book expense is 100%, tax deduction is 50% // Addback = 50% of meals/entertainment expense expenses_not_deducted += result.m1_meals_entertainment_50pct;
// Book-tax depreciation difference (if book > tax) // Tax depreciation (MACRS/179/Bonus) typically exceeds book (straight-line) // If book depreciation > tax depreciation (rare), addback the difference // Most common: tax depreciation > book, so this is usually 0 or negative double depreciation_addback = Math.max(0.0, result.m1_book_depreciation - result.depreciation); expenses_not_deducted += depreciation_addback;
// Federal income tax (already counted in line 2, don't double-count) // Other common items: penalties, fines, lobbying, club dues, etc.
result.m1_expenses_not_deducted = expenses_not_deducted;
// ======================================== // Schedule M-1 Line 6: Subtotal (sum of lines 1-5) // ======================================== result.m1_subtotal = result.m1_net_income_per_books + result.m1_federal_tax_per_books + result.m1_excess_capital_losses + result.m1_income_not_on_books + result.m1_expenses_not_deducted;
// ======================================== // Schedule M-1 Line 7: Income on Books NOT Included on Return // ======================================== // Tax-exempt interest (tax-exempt municipal bonds) // On books as income, but not taxable result.m1_income_not_on_return = result.m1_tax_exempt_interest;
// ======================================== // Schedule M-1 Line 8: Deductions on Return NOT Charged Against Books // ======================================== double deductions_not_on_books = 0.0;
// Tax depreciation exceeding book depreciation (most common case) // MACRS/179/Bonus typically > straight-line book depreciation double tax_depreciation_excess = Math.max(0.0, result.depreciation - result.m1_book_depreciation); deductions_not_on_books += tax_depreciation_excess;
// Capital loss carryover from prior years (deductible for tax, not on books) deductions_not_on_books += result.m1_capital_loss_carryover;
result.m1_deductions_not_on_books = deductions_not_on_books;
// ======================================== // Schedule M-1 Line 9: Total (sum of lines 7-8) // ======================================== result.m1_total_deductions = result.m1_income_not_on_return + result.m1_deductions_not_on_books;
// ======================================== // Schedule M-1 Line 10: Reconciled Income (line 6 - line 9) // ======================================== // This MUST equal taxable income (Form 1120 line 28) result.m1_reconciled_income = result.m1_subtotal - result.m1_total_deductions;
// Validation: Check if reconciliation matches taxable income double reconciliation_difference = Math.abs(result.m1_reconciled_income - result.taxable_income);
// If difference > $1, log warning (should match exactly) if (reconciliation_difference > 1.0) { // Schedule M-1 reconciliation error // M-1 line 10 should equal taxable income // Difference may indicate missing book-tax adjustments }
Schedule M-1 reconciles net income per books with income per return.
Common book-tax differences:
**Temporary Differences** (timing - reverse in future years): - Depreciation (MACRS/bonus vs. straight-line book) - Section 179 expense (immediate vs. capitalized for books) - Prepaid expenses (deductible when paid for tax, recognized over time for books) - Accrued liabilities (deductible when accrued for books, when paid for tax)
**Permanent Differences** (never reverse): - Tax-exempt interest (income for books, not taxable) - Federal income tax (expense for books, not deductible) - 50% of meals and entertainment (100% expense for books, 50% deductible) - Penalties and fines (expense for books, not deductible) - Life insurance premiums (expense for books, not deductible if corporation is beneficiary) - Lobbying expenses (expense for books, not deductible) - Club dues (expense for books, not deductible)
Schedule M-1 is required for corporations with: - Total assets >= $10 million at end of year
Smaller corporations may file simplified Schedule M-1 or omit if assets < $250K.
Reference: Form 1120 Schedule M-1 Instructions Reference: Publication 542 - Corporations Reference: Regulations § 1.6012-2 (Filing requirements)
