Schedule M-2 analyzes changes in unappropriated retained earnings.
**Components**:
**Increases to Retained Earnings**: - Net income per books (from Schedule M-1) - Prior period adjustments (corrections to prior years) - Accounting changes - Error corrections
**Decreases to Retained Earnings**: - Cash dividends paid to shareholders - Stock dividends distributed - Property distributions - Treasury stock purchases - Stock redemptions
**Required for**: - Corporations with total assets >= $250,000 at end of year
**Not required for**: - Smaller corporations (assets < $250,000) - S corporations (use different schedule)
**Notes**: - Schedule M-2 tracks only UNAPPROPRIATED retained earnings - Appropriated retained earnings (reserves) not included - Should reconcile with Schedule L (balance sheet) line 25 - Reflects book accounting, not tax basis
Reference: Form 1120 Schedule M-2 Instructions Reference: Publication 542 - Corporations Reference: Regulations § 1.6012-2 (Filing requirements)
