// ======================================== // Current Year NOL Generation // ========================================
result.taxable_income_before_nol = result.taxable_income;
// Current year NOL (absolute value of negative taxable income) result.nol_current_year = Math.abs(result.taxable_income);
// No NOL deduction this year (loss year, not profit year) result.nol_deduction_allowed = 0.0; result.nol_80pct_limitation = 0.0;
// Taxable income remains at $0 (cannot be negative on return) result.taxable_income_after_nol = 0.0; result.taxable_income = 0.0;
// Total NOL carryforward = prior years + current year result.nol_carryforward_to_future_years = result.nol_carryforward_from_prior_years + result.nol_current_year;
// No tax liability (loss year) result.federal_tax = 0.0; result.refund_or_owed = result.total_payments; // Refund all payments
Current year NOL (negative taxable income).
**NOL Generation**: - Corporation has loss (expenses exceed income) - NOL = absolute value of negative taxable income - No tax owed in NOL year - Estimated payments refunded
**Post-TCJA Carryforward**: - Indefinite carryforward (no expiration) - No carryback (general rule) - Can offset 80% of future taxable income
**CARES Act Carryback** (2018-2020 NOLs): - 5-year carryback available - Must elect carryback vs. carryforward - Carryback not implemented in this version
**NOL Calculation**: - Start with taxable income before NOL - If negative, equals current year NOL - Add to prior year NOL carryforward - Total carries forward indefinitely
Reference: IRC § 172(a)(1) - NOL deduction defined Reference: IRC § 172(b)(1) - Carryforward period (indefinite) Reference: CARES Act § 2303 - Temporary 5-year carryback
Calculate foreign tax credit with limitation and carryover tracking. Prevents double taxation of foreign source income.
result.foreign_source_income > 0 Has foreign source taxable income
result.foreign_taxes_paid > 0 Has foreign income taxes paid or accrued
result.foreign_tax_credit_carryforward > 0 || result.foreign_tax_credit_carryback > 0 Has FTC carryover from other years
Y Y
// ======================================== // Foreign Tax Credit Limitation (IRC § 904) // ========================================
// Total taxable income for FTC purposes // Use taxable income after NOL but before FTC result.total_taxable_income_for_ftc = result.taxable_income;
// FTC Limitation Formula: // US Tax × (Foreign Source Income / Total Taxable Income) // // This ensures credit doesn't exceed US tax that would be owed // on the foreign income if earned domestically
if (result.total_taxable_income_for_ftc > 0) { double foreign_income_ratio = result.foreign_source_income / result.total_taxable_income_for_ftc;
result.foreign_tax_credit_limitation = result.federal_tax * foreign_income_ratio; } else { result.foreign_tax_credit_limitation = 0.0; }
// ======================================== // FTC Allowed (Lesser of Taxes Paid or Limitation) // ========================================
// Current year FTC = lesser of: // 1. Foreign taxes actually paid // 2. FTC limitation (US tax on foreign income) double current_year_ftc = Math.min( result.foreign_taxes_paid, result.foreign_tax_credit_limitation );
// Add carryforward from prior years (within 10-year window) double total_ftc_available = current_year_ftc + result.foreign_tax_credit_carryforward;
// FTC allowed cannot exceed limitation result.foreign_tax_credit_allowed = Math.min( total_ftc_available, result.foreign_tax_credit_limitation );
// ======================================== // Excess FTC (Carryback/Carryforward) // ========================================
// If foreign taxes paid > limitation, excess carries over double current_year_excess = result.foreign_taxes_paid - result.foreign_tax_credit_limitation;
if (current_year_excess > 0) { // Excess can be carried back 1 year or forward 10 years // For simplicity, we track carryforward only (carryback requires prior year data) result.excess_foreign_tax_credit = current_year_excess; } else { result.excess_foreign_tax_credit = 0.0; }
// Update carryforward for next year // = Prior carryforward - amount used this year + new excess double carryforward_used = result.foreign_tax_credit_allowed - current_year_ftc;
result.foreign_tax_credit_carryforward = Math.max(0.0, result.foreign_tax_credit_carryforward - carryforward_used) + result.excess_foreign_tax_credit;
// ======================================== // Update Federal Tax (after FTC) // ========================================
// FTC is a direct credit against federal tax // Reduces tax dollar-for-dollar (unlike deductions) result.federal_tax = Math.max(0.0, result.federal_tax - result.foreign_tax_credit_allowed);
Foreign Tax Credit (FTC) calculation with limitation.
**Purpose**: - Prevents double taxation of foreign source income - Allows credit for foreign income taxes paid - Credit (not deduction) reduces US tax dollar-for-dollar
**FTC Limitation** (IRC § 904): - Credit cannot exceed US tax on foreign income - Formula: US Tax × (Foreign Income / Total Income) - Prevents using foreign taxes to offset US source income tax
**Example**: - Total taxable income: $1,000,000 - Foreign source income: $200,000 (20%) - US tax (21%): $210,000 - FTC limitation: $210,000 × 20% = $42,000 - Foreign taxes paid: $50,000 - FTC allowed: $42,000 (limited) - Excess: $8,000 (carryforward/carryback)
**Carryback/Carryforward**: - Excess FTC: 1 year carryback, 10 years carryforward - Use carrybacks/carryforwards subject to same limitation - Carryovers expire after 10 years
**Separate Limitation Baskets** (IRC § 904(d)): - Passive income basket (simplified implementation) - General category income basket - Each basket has separate limitation calculation - Prevents cross-crediting between baskets
**Form 1118 Requirements**: - Schedule A: Foreign tax paid/accrued - Schedule B: Foreign source income - Schedule C: FTC limitation calculation - Schedule D: Allocation of income/taxes
Reference: IRC § 901 - Taxes of foreign countries Reference: IRC § 904 - Limitation on credit Reference: IRC § 905 - Applicable rules Reference: Form 1118 Instructions Reference: Regulations § 1.904-1 (Limitation calculation)
Y N Y
// Can use carryforward even if no current year foreign taxes
result.total_taxable_income_for_ftc = result.taxable_income;
if (result.total_taxable_income_for_ftc > 0) { double foreign_income_ratio = result.foreign_source_income / result.total_taxable_income_for_ftc;
result.foreign_tax_credit_limitation = result.federal_tax * foreign_income_ratio; } else { result.foreign_tax_credit_limitation = 0.0; }
// Use carryforward up to limitation result.foreign_tax_credit_allowed = Math.min( result.foreign_tax_credit_carryforward, result.foreign_tax_credit_limitation );
// Update carryforward result.foreign_tax_credit_carryforward = result.foreign_tax_credit_carryforward - result.foreign_tax_credit_allowed;
// Apply credit result.federal_tax = Math.max(0.0, result.federal_tax - result.foreign_tax_credit_allowed);
