A US person is a "US shareholder" if they own 10% or more of the voting power of a foreign corporation.
**US Person Defined (IRC § 7701(a)(30))**: - US citizen or resident - Domestic partnership - Domestic corporation - Estate (not foreign estate) - Trust (certain US trusts)
**Direct Ownership**: - Stock owned directly by the US person - No intermediary entities - Easiest case - straightforward ownership test
**US Shareholder Consequences**: - Must file Form 5471 (Category 4 or 5) - Subject to Subpart F income inclusions - Subject to GILTI inclusions - Must report pro-rata share of CFC income
