US shareholder status is determined using constructive ownership rules.
**Indirect Ownership (IRC § 958(a)(2))**: - Ownership through foreign entities (partnerships, corporations, trusts) - Pro-rata share of entity's ownership - Example: US person owns 50% of Partnership; Partnership owns 30% of CFC → US person has 15% indirect ownership (50% × 30%)
**Constructive Ownership (IRC § 958(b), § 318)**: 1. **Family Attribution**: Stock owned by family members - Spouse, children, grandchildren, parents - NOT siblings 2. **Entity Attribution**: Stock owned by/from entities - From partnership: proportional to interest - From estate/trust: proportional to beneficial interest - From corporation: if own 50%+ 3. **Option Attribution**: Stock acquirable via option/convertible security
**Total Ownership Calculation**: - Total = Direct + Indirect + Constructive - If total ≥ 10%, US shareholder status applies - Even if direct ownership is 0%
