// ======================================== // Calculate Total Ownership - Value // ======================================== form_5471.total_ownership_value = form_5471.direct_ownership_value + form_5471.indirect_ownership_value + form_5471.constructive_ownership_value;
// Cap at 100% if (form_5471.total_ownership_value > 1.0) { form_5471.total_ownership_value = 1.0; }
// ======================================== // Calculate Stock Ownership for Schedule A // ======================================== form_5471.sched_a_voting_stock_owned_pct = form_5471.total_ownership_voting; form_5471.sched_a_total_value_stock_owned_pct = form_5471.total_ownership_value;
Total ownership = Direct + Indirect + Constructive.
**Direct Ownership (IRC § 958(a)(1))**: - Stock owned directly by US person - No intermediaries
**Indirect Ownership (IRC § 958(a)(2))**: - Ownership through foreign entities - Proportional to US person's interest in intermediary entity - Example: US Corp owns 60% of Foreign Partnership (FP) FP owns 40% of CFC → US Corp has 24% indirect ownership (60% × 40%)
**Constructive Ownership (IRC § 958(b) + § 318)**: 1. **Family Attribution (§ 318(a)(1))**: - Stock owned by spouse, children, grandchildren, parents - NOT siblings 2. **Entity Attribution (§ 318(a)(2), (a)(3))**: - From partnership: proportional to partnership interest - From estate/trust: proportional to actuarial interest - From corporation: if own ≥50% of value - To entity: reverse attribution 3. **Option Attribution (§ 318(a)(4))**: - Stock subject to option to acquire - Convertible securities
**Important Rules**: - Stock cannot be attributed twice (no "chain" attribution) - Family attribution does NOT apply for certain tests - Total ownership capped at 100%
**Form 5471 Schedule A**: - Report both voting and value percentages - Include footnotes explaining attribution
