Form 5471 Schedule A: Stock of the Foreign Corporation
Calculate stock ownership percentages: - Voting stock % = Shares owned ÷ Total shares outstanding - Total value stock % = Value of shares owned ÷ Total value of all shares
U.S. Shareholder Definition (IRC § 951(b)): A U.S. person who owns 10% or more of the total combined voting power of all classes of stock entitled to vote.
CFC Definition (IRC § 957(a)): A foreign corporation in which more than 50% of: - Total combined voting power of all classes of stock entitled to vote, or - Total value of the stock is owned (directly, indirectly, or constructively) by U.S. shareholders on any day during the tax year.
Stock Basis (IRC § 961): U.S. shareholders must track basis in CFC stock for: - Increases from Subpart F inclusions and GILTI - Decreases from distributions of PTEP
