// Schedule H: Current Earnings and Profits Calculation
// Start with net income per books (Schedule C) form_5471.sched_h_net_income_per_books = form_5471.sched_c_net_income;
// Adjust for depreciation differences (book vs U.S. tax rules) // Positive adjustment = U.S. depreciation > book depreciation (increases E&P) // Negative adjustment = U.S. depreciation < book depreciation (decreases E&P) double ep_before_taxes = form_5471.sched_h_net_income_per_books + form_5471.sched_h_us_depreciation_adjustment + form_5471.sched_h_other_adjustments;
// Subtract foreign income taxes (they reduce E&P) form_5471.sched_h_current_earnings_and_profits = ep_before_taxes - form_5471.sched_h_foreign_taxes_paid;
// Handle E&P deficit if (form_5471.sched_h_current_earnings_and_profits < 0) { form_5471.sched_h_current_year_deficit = Math.abs(form_5471.sched_h_current_earnings_and_profits); } else { form_5471.sched_h_current_year_deficit = 0.0; }
// Pass current E&P to Schedule J form_5471.sched_j_current_year_ep = form_5471.sched_h_current_earnings_and_profits;
Form 5471 Schedule H: Current Earnings and Profits (E&P)
Current E&P Calculation: 1. Start with net income per books (Schedule C) 2. Add: U.S. depreciation adjustments - If U.S. depreciation > book depreciation: positive adjustment - If U.S. depreciation < book depreciation: negative adjustment 3. Add/subtract: Other E&P adjustments - Tax-exempt income (increases E&P) - Nondeductible expenses (decreases E&P) - Federal income tax (decreases E&P for domestic corps) 4. Subtract: Foreign income taxes paid (Schedule E) 5. Result: Current year E&P
E&P vs. Taxable Income Differences: - Municipal bond interest: Included in E&P, excluded from taxable income - Depreciation: E&P uses ADS (slower), taxable income uses MACRS (faster) - Foreign taxes: Reduce E&P, but credited against U.S. tax - Dividends received deduction: Reduces taxable income, not E&P
Current E&P Priority: Current E&P is applied to distributions BEFORE accumulated E&P. If current E&P is sufficient to cover distributions, entire distribution is a dividend regardless of accumulated E&P deficit.
Reference: IRC § 312 - E&P calculation rules Reference: IRC § 316 - Dividend definition Reference: Treas. Reg. § 1.312-6 - E&P ordering rules Reference: Form 5471 Instructions, Schedule H
