// Schedule J: Accumulated Earnings and Profits
// Start with beginning accumulated E&P double accumulated_ep = form_5471.sched_j_beginning_accumulated_ep;
// Add current year E&P (or subtract current year deficit) accumulated_ep += form_5471.sched_j_current_year_ep;
// Subtract distributions accumulated_ep -= form_5471.sched_j_distributions;
// Adjust for PTEP reclassifications // When PTEP is distributed, it's removed from accumulated E&P // (it was already taxed to U.S. shareholder) accumulated_ep += form_5471.sched_j_reclassifications;
// Set ending accumulated E&P form_5471.sched_j_ending_accumulated_ep = accumulated_ep;
Form 5471 Schedule J: Accumulated Earnings and Profits (E&P)
Accumulated E&P Calculation: 1. Beginning accumulated E&P (prior year ending balance) 2. + Current year E&P (from Schedule H) 3. - Distributions during the year 4. +/- Reclassifications to/from PTEP 5. = Ending accumulated E&P
Distribution Ordering Rules (IRC § 316(a)): Distributions are treated as coming from: 1. FIRST: Current E&P (dividends, taxable to extent of current E&P) 2. SECOND: Accumulated E&P (dividends, taxable to extent available) 3. THIRD: Return of basis (nontaxable, reduces shareholder basis) 4. FOURTH: Gain from sale of stock (capital gain)
PTEP Impact: Previously Taxed Earnings and Profits (PTEP) are tracked separately. When PTEP is distributed: - Distribution is NOT taxable (already taxed via Subpart F or GILTI) - Accumulated E&P is reduced - Shareholder stock basis is reduced
Negative Accumulated E&P: A deficit in accumulated E&P does NOT prevent current E&P from being a dividend. Current E&P and accumulated E&P are tested separately.
Reference: IRC § 316(a) - Dividend definition and ordering Reference: IRC § 959 - PTEP exclusion from gross income Reference: Treas. Reg. § 1.316-2 - Distribution ordering rules Reference: Form 5471 Instructions, Schedule J
