PTEP Tracking: Section 951(a) - Subpart F Income
Subpart F Income (IRC § 952): U.S. shareholders of CFCs must include in income their pro rata share of Subpart F income, even if not distributed.
Common Subpart F income categories: - Foreign base company sales income (buying from/selling to related parties) - Foreign base company services income (services for related parties) - Foreign personal holding company income (passive income: dividends, interest, rents, royalties) - Insurance income - International boycott income - Illegal bribes, kickbacks, or payments to officials
PTEP Creation (IRC § 959(a)): When Subpart F income is included in U.S. shareholder's gross income, it creates PTEP in the CFC equal to the amount included.
Stock Basis Increase (IRC § 961(a)): U.S. shareholder's basis in CFC stock is increased by the amount of Subpart F income included in gross income.
PTEP Distribution (IRC § 959(a)): When CFC distributes PTEP to U.S. shareholder: - Distribution is NOT included in gross income (already taxed) - U.S. shareholder's stock basis is decreased (IRC § 961(b)) - CFC's accumulated E&P is reduced
Reference: IRC § 951(a) - Subpart F inclusion Reference: IRC § 952 - Subpart F income definition Reference: IRC § 959 - PTEP exclusion from income Reference: IRC § 961 - Stock basis adjustments Reference: Form 5471 Instructions
