// Add current year GILTI inclusions ptep_951A += form_5471.ptep_section_951A_gilti_additions;
// Subtract distributions of Section 951A PTEP ptep_951A -= form_5471.ptep_section_951A_gilti_distributions;
// Ending balance form_5471.ptep_section_951A_gilti_end = ptep_951A;
// Stock basis adjustment: Increase basis by GILTI inclusion form_5471.stock_basis_gilti_inclusion = form_5471.ptep_section_951A_gilti_additions;
PTEP Tracking: Section 951A - GILTI (Global Intangible Low-Taxed Income)
GILTI (IRC § 951A): Added by Tax Cuts and Jobs Act (TCJA) 2017, effective 2018. U.S. shareholders of CFCs must include in income their pro rata share of GILTI, even if not distributed.
GILTI Calculation: 1. Net CFC tested income (income excluding Subpart F, ECI, certain high-taxed income) 2. Minus: 10% of qualified business asset investment (QBAI) 3. = GILTI (taxed currently to U.S. shareholder)
GILTI Deduction (IRC § 250): C corporations get 50% deduction for GILTI (37.5% after 2025). Effective tax rate: 10.5% (13.125% after 2025) before foreign tax credits.
GILTI Foreign Tax Credit (IRC § 960(d)): 80% of foreign taxes paid on GILTI income can be credited.
PTEP Creation (IRC § 959(a)): GILTI inclusions create Section 951A PTEP, tracked separately from Section 951(a) Subpart F PTEP.
Stock Basis Increase (IRC § 961(a)): U.S. shareholder's basis in CFC stock is increased by GILTI inclusion.
PTEP Distribution (IRC § 959(a)): Section 951A PTEP distributions are excluded from gross income (already taxed via GILTI), and reduce stock basis.
PTEP Ordering: Section 951(a) PTEP is distributed BEFORE Section 951A PTEP.
Reference: IRC § 951A - GILTI inclusion Reference: IRC § 250 - GILTI deduction (50% for C corps) Reference: IRC § 959 - PTEP exclusion from income Reference: IRC § 960(d) - GILTI foreign tax credit Reference: IRC § 961 - Stock basis adjustments Reference: Form 5471 Instructions
