// Reclassify PTEP distributions out of accumulated E&P form_5471.sched_j_reclassifications = -form_5471.stock_basis_distributions_from_ptep;
Stock Basis Adjustments and PTEP Distribution Ordering
Stock Basis Adjustments (IRC § 961):
Increases to Basis: - Subpart F income inclusions (IRC § 951(a)) - GILTI inclusions (IRC § 951A) - Pro rata share of CFC's increase in E&P from investments in U.S. property
Decreases to Basis: - Distributions of PTEP (excluded from income under IRC § 959) - Pro rata share of CFC's decrease in E&P from investments in U.S. property
PTEP Distribution Ordering (IRC § 959(c)): Distributions are treated as coming from (in order): 1. Section 959(c)(1) PTEP - Previously taxed Subpart F income 2. Section 959(c)(2) PTEP - Previously taxed under other provisions 3. Section 959(c)(3) - Other E&P (currently taxable as dividend)
Within Section 959(c)(1), ordering is: 1. Section 951(a)(1)(A) PTEP - Subpart F income (priority) 2. Section 951A PTEP - GILTI (after Subpart F PTEP exhausted)
Within each category, LIFO (last-in-first-out) ordering applies by tax year.
Impact on Accumulated E&P: PTEP distributions reduce accumulated E&P but are not taxable dividends. Must track PTEP separately to properly characterize distributions.
Form 5471 Reporting: Schedule J shows reclassification adjustments for PTEP distributions. Separate PTEP schedules may be required for complex situations.
