// Calculate total Foreign Base Company Income (IRC § 954) form_5471.foreign_base_company_income = form_5471.foreign_personal_holding_company_income + form_5471.foreign_base_company_sales_income + form_5471.foreign_base_company_services_income;
Foreign Base Company Income (IRC § 954)
FBCI is the sum of: 1. Foreign Personal Holding Company Income (IRC § 954(c)) - Passive income: dividends, interest, rents, royalties, capital gains
2. Foreign Base Company Sales Income (IRC § 954(d)) - Related party sales of property manufactured outside CFC country
3. Foreign Base Company Services Income (IRC § 954(e)) - Related party services performed outside CFC country
4. Foreign Base Company Oil-Related Income (IRC § 954(g)) - Not implemented in this version
FBCI is a component of Subpart F income, which is taxed currently to U.S. shareholders even if not distributed.
Reference: IRC § 954 - Foreign base company income defined Reference: Form 5471 Instructions
Calculate Foreign Base Company Sales Income per IRC § 954(d).
FBCI Sales Income includes income from: - Purchase of property from related person and sale to any person, OR - Purchase of property from any person and sale to related person
WHERE the property is manufactured outside the CFC's country of incorporation AND not for use in the CFC's country of incorporation.
form_5471.sched_m_sales_to_related > 0 || form_5471.sched_m_purchases_from_related > 0
Has sales to or purchases from related parties
form_5471.fbci_sales_manufactured_in_cfc_country Property manufactured in CFC country of incorporation
form_5471.fbci_sales_for_use_in_cfc_country Property for use in CFC country of incorporation
