Foreign Base Company Sales Income (IRC § 954(d))
FBCI Sales Income includes income from property transactions where:
1. Related Party Requirement: - CFC purchases from related person and sells to any person, OR - CFC purchases from any person and sells to related person
2. Manufacturing/Use Exception Does NOT Apply: - Property NOT manufactured in CFC's country of incorporation, AND - Property NOT for use in CFC's country of incorporation
Related Person Definition (IRC § 954(d)(3)): - Commonly controlled (>50% ownership) - Attribution rules of IRC § 318 apply
Manufacturing Exception (IRC § 954(d)(1)(A)): If CFC manufactures the property in its country of incorporation, sales income is NOT FBCI (active business exception).
Same Country Exception (IRC § 954(d)(1)(B)): If property sold for use in CFC's country of incorporation, sales income is NOT FBCI.
Branch Rule (IRC § 954(d)(2)): If CFC has branch that manufactures property in different country, may create FBCI even if sold to unrelated party.
Reference: IRC § 954(d) - Foreign base company sales income Reference: Treas. Reg. § 1.954-3 - Sales income regulations Reference: Form 5471 Instructions
