If the CFC manufactures the property in its country of incorporation, the sales income is NOT Foreign Base Company Sales Income.
This is the "manufacturing exception" - encourages CFCs to engage in active manufacturing rather than just purchasing and reselling.
Manufacturing includes substantial transformation of the property, not just minor assembly or packaging.
