Foreign Personal Holding Company Income (IRC § 954(c))
FPHCI is the passive income of a CFC, including:
1. Dividends (IRC § 954(c)(1)(A)): - Dividends received from stock ownership - Exception: Look-through rule for related CFC dividends (IRC § 954(c)(6)) - Exception: Dividends from less than 25% owned corporations
2. Interest (IRC § 954(c)(1)(B)): - Interest from loans, bonds, notes - Exception: Export financing interest (IRC § 954(c)(2)(B)) - Exception: Active financing income (IRC § 954(h), (i))
3. Rents (IRC § 954(c)(1)(A)): - Rents from real or personal property - Exception: Active rental income with substantial services
4. Royalties (IRC § 954(c)(1)(A)): - Royalties from intangible property licenses - Exception: Active royalties related to CFC's active business
5. Net Capital Gains (IRC § 954(c)(1)(B)): - Gains from sale of stock, securities, partnership interests - Exception: Gains from sale of active business assets
6. Commodities Gains (IRC § 954(c)(1)(C)): - Gains from commodities transactions - Exception: Hedges of active business risks
7. Foreign Currency Gains (IRC § 954(c)(1)(D)): - Gains from foreign currency transactions - Exception: Business hedges, certain customer transactions
Same Country Exception (IRC § 954(c)(3)): Dividends and interest from related CFCs in same country may be excluded.
Active Rents and Royalties Exception (IRC § 954(c)(2)(A)): Rents and royalties derived in active business may be excluded.
Reference: IRC § 954(c) - Foreign personal holding company income Reference: Treas. Reg. § 1.954-2 - FPHCI regulations Reference: Form 5471 Instructions
