// Full inclusion rule: ALL gross income is Subpart F form_5471.subpart_f_income = form_5471.subpart_f_gross_income; form_5471.subpart_f_de_minimis_applied = false; form_5471.subpart_f_full_inclusion_applied = true;
// Still subject to E&P limitation form_5471.subpart_f_ep_limitation = form_5471.sched_h_current_earnings_and_profits;
form_5471.subpart_f_after_ep_limitation = Math.min(form_5471.subpart_f_income, form_5471.subpart_f_ep_limitation);
form_5471.subpart_f_income = form_5471.subpart_f_after_ep_limitation;
Full Inclusion Rule (IRC § 954(b)(3)(B))
If Subpart F income before limitations exceeds 70% of gross income, then ALL gross income is treated as Subpart F income.
This is an anti-abuse rule to prevent CFCs from characterizing most income as Subpart F while claiming a small amount is active.
The full inclusion rule overrides the de minimis rule.
However, the E&P limitation still applies - cannot include more than current year earnings and profits.
Reference: IRC § 954(b)(3)(B) Reference: IRC § 952(c) - E&P limitation Reference: Form 5471 Instructions
