Normal Subpart F Income Calculation
When neither de minimis nor full inclusion rules apply, Subpart F income equals the calculated amount, subject to the current E&P limitation.
E&P Limitation (IRC § 952(c)): Subpart F income cannot exceed current year earnings and profits.
If current E&P is negative or zero, Subpart F income is zero.
If current E&P is less than calculated Subpart F income, Subpart F income is limited to current E&P.
Purpose: Prevent inclusion of income that has not been earned economically (e.g., due to high foreign tax deductions).
