High-Tax Exception (IRC § 954(b)(4))
Subpart F income is excluded if the effective foreign tax rate exceeds 90% of the maximum U.S. corporate tax rate.
Current Calculation (2025): - U.S. corporate rate: 21% - 90% of U.S. rate: 18.9% - If foreign effective rate > 18.9%, exception applies
Effective Foreign Tax Rate: = Foreign income taxes paid / Subpart F income
Foreign taxes include: - Foreign income taxes (not VAT, sales tax, etc.) - Withheld at source - Paid by CFC on Subpart F income
Election Required: Taxpayer must elect to apply high-tax exception. Election is annual and applies to all CFCs.
Impact: - Subpart F income excluded from current U.S. taxation - Income becomes tested income (potentially subject to GILTI) - Foreign taxes may be creditable under GILTI rules
TCJA Changes: Pre-2018: High-tax exception was optional election. Post-2017: Exception still available but interaction with GILTI creates new planning considerations.
Reference: IRC § 954(b)(4) - High-tax exception Reference: Treas. Reg. § 1.954-1(d) - High-tax exception regulations Reference: Form 5471 Instructions Reference: Form 8993 (GILTI calculation if exception applies)
