// Store tested income for this CFC form_5471.tested_income = tested_income; form_5471.tested_loss = 0.0;
// Calculate pro-rata share for U.S. shareholder double ownership_pct = form_5471.sched_a_voting_stock_owned_pct; form_5471.pro_rata_share_tested_income = tested_income * ownership_pct;
Tested Income Calculation (IRC § 951A(c)(2)(A))
Tested Income Definition: Tested income is the excess of: (1) Gross income of the CFC (excluding Subpart F income, effectively connected income, dividends from related CFCs, and foreign oil/gas extraction income), OVER (2) Deductions properly allocable to such gross income
High-Tax Exclusion (IRC § 951A(c)(2)(A)(i)(III)): Income subject to foreign tax at an effective rate greater than 90% of the U.S. corporate tax rate is excluded from tested income. - U.S. rate: 21% - 90% of U.S. rate: 18.9% - Therefore, income taxed at foreign rate > 18.9% is excluded
Subpart F Income Excluded: Income already included under Subpart F (IRC § 952) is excluded from tested income to prevent double taxation.
Effectively Connected Income Excluded: Income effectively connected with a U.S. trade or business is taxed directly and excluded from GILTI.
Pro-Rata Share: U.S. shareholder includes pro-rata share based on stock ownership percentage (by voting power or value, whichever is greater).
Reference: IRC § 951A(c)(2)(A) - Tested income Reference: IRC § 951A(c)(2)(A)(i)(III) - High-tax exclusion Reference: Treas. Reg. § 1.951A-2(c) - Tested income
