// CFC has a loss double net_loss = -form_5471.sched_c_net_income;
// Tested loss (absolute value of negative income) form_5471.tested_loss = net_loss; form_5471.tested_income = 0.0;
// Pro-rata share of loss double ownership_pct = form_5471.sched_a_voting_stock_owned_pct; double pro_rata_loss = net_loss * ownership_pct;
// Tested losses reduce net tested income in aggregate form_5471.pro_rata_share_tested_income = -pro_rata_loss;
Tested Loss (IRC § 951A(c)(2)(B))
Tested Loss Definition: Tested loss is the excess of deductions (including taxes) properly allocable to gross income (excluding Subpart F income and ECI) over such gross income.
Netting of Tested Income and Tested Losses: A U.S. shareholder's GILTI is calculated by netting together: - All tested income from all CFCs (positive amounts), MINUS - All tested losses from all CFCs (negative amounts)
No Current Deduction for Tested Losses: Tested losses reduce GILTI but do not create a deduction if they exceed tested income. Tested losses cannot create or increase a net operating loss.
Carryforward of Excess Tested Losses: If aggregate tested losses exceed aggregate tested income, the excess is not carried forward to future years. Tested losses are "use it or lose it" in the current year.
CFC Loss in Local Currency: For CFCs with functional currency other than USD, losses must be translated at the average exchange rate for the year.
Reference: IRC § 951A(c)(2)(B) - Tested loss Reference: Treas. Reg. § 1.951A-2(c) - Tested loss calculation Reference: Treas. Reg. § 1.951A-6 - Rules for tested losses
