// Calculate 10% deemed return on QBAI double qbai = form_5471.qualified_business_asset_investment; double deemed_return_rate = 0.10; // 10% per IRC § 951A(b)(2)(B)
// Net deemed tangible income return = 10% × QBAI double ndtir = qbai * deemed_return_rate;
// Pro-rata share for U.S. shareholder double ownership_pct = form_5471.sched_a_voting_stock_owned_pct; form_5471.pro_rata_share_qbai = qbai * ownership_pct;
// Store for aggregation across all CFCs double pro_rata_ndtir = ndtir * ownership_pct; result.gilti_net_deemed_tangible_income_return += pro_rata_ndtir;
Net Deemed Tangible Income Return (NDTIR) - IRC § 951A(b)(2)
NDTIR Calculation: NDTIR = 10% × Qualified Business Asset Investment (QBAI)
Qualified Business Asset Investment (QBAI) - IRC § 951A(d): QBAI is the average of the CFC's aggregate adjusted bases in tangible property: (1) Used in a trade or business of the CFC, AND (2) For which a deduction is allowed under IRC § 167 (depreciation)
Average Adjusted Basis: QBAI = (Beginning basis + Ending basis) / 2
Measured quarterly for more precision: QBAI = Sum of adjusted bases at end of each quarter / 4
Tangible Property Includes: - Buildings and structures - Machinery and equipment - Furniture and fixtures - Vehicles - Computer hardware (but not software)
Excluded from QBAI: - Intangible property (patents, trademarks, goodwill, software) - Land (not depreciable) - Inventory - Financial assets (cash, securities, loans) - Property held for investment (not used in trade or business)
Basis Adjustments: - Reduced by depreciation claimed - Adjusted for impairment, revaluations under local GAAP - Must use U.S. tax basis (not local GAAP basis) - Alternative depreciation system (ADS) basis required
10% Return Rationale: Congress provided this deduction to exclude routine returns on tangible capital from GILTI. The 10% return represents normal business returns from tangible assets (factories, equipment, etc.). Returns above 10% are presumed to derive from intangible assets (IP, know-how, etc.) and are subject to GILTI.
Impact on GILTI: GILTI = Net Tested Income - NDTIR Higher QBAI = Lower GILTI inclusion
Incentive for Tangible Investment: Encourages U.S. multinationals to invest in tangible property abroad (creates jobs, facilities) rather than shifting intangible income to low-tax jurisdictions.
Reference: IRC § 951A(b)(2) - Net deemed tangible income return Reference: IRC § 951A(d) - Qualified business asset investment Reference: Treas. Reg. § 1.951A-3 - QBAI calculation Reference: Form 8992 Instructions - QBAI computation
