No QBAI - No Tangible Property Deduction
CFC has no qualified business asset investment (no tangible depreciable property used in trade or business).
Common scenarios: - Holding company (owns stock/intangibles, no operating assets) - Service company (labor-based, minimal equipment) - IP holding company (owns patents, trademarks - intangibles) - Financial services company (assets are financial instruments)
Impact: No NDTIR deduction means all tested income is subject to GILTI. GILTI = Net Tested Income - 0
This captures the policy goal: income from intangible property (IP, brand value, algorithms) is subject to GILTI, while income from tangible business operations gets a 10% return exemption.
Reference: IRC § 951A(b)(2) Reference: IRC § 951A(d)
