U.S. shareholder has net tested income but no QBAI. All net tested income is included as GILTI.
This occurs when CFCs have no tangible depreciable property: - IP holding companies - Service businesses with minimal equipment - Financial services companies
Full GILTI exposure reflects congressional intent to tax income from intangible property that has been shifted to low-tax jurisdictions.
Reference: IRC § 951A(b)(1)
