Aggregate tested losses from CFCs equal or exceed aggregate tested income. No GILTI inclusion.
Tested Loss Limitation: Excess tested losses (beyond tested income) do NOT carry forward to future years. They are lost.
Tested losses cannot: - Create a net operating loss (NOL) - Be carried back or forward - Generate a deduction
Planning Consideration: Companies may accelerate tested income or defer tested losses to utilize losses before they expire.
Reference: IRC § 951A(c)(2)(B) - Tested loss limitation Reference: Treas. Reg. § 1.951A-6 - Treatment of tested losses
