Section 250 GILTI Deduction - C Corporations (IRC § 250(a)(1)(B))
Deduction Amount (2018-2025): C corporations may deduct 50% of GILTI inclusion amount.
Effective Tax Rate on GILTI: - Statutory corporate rate: 21% - GILTI after 50% deduction: 21% × 50% = 10.5% effective rate - With 80% foreign tax credit: Can be lower or zero
Deduction Amount (After 2025): Deduction rate reduced to 37.5% for tax years after December 31, 2025. - Effective rate: 21% × 62.5% = 13.125%
Taxable Income Limitation (IRC § 250(a)(2)): Section 250 deduction cannot exceed taxable income (before Section 250).
Formula: Section 250 deduction = Lesser of: (1) 50% of GILTI inclusion (37.5% after 2025), OR (2) Taxable income (before Section 250 deduction)
If taxable income limitation applies, deduction is reduced proportionally between GILTI deduction and FDII deduction (if applicable).
No Carryover: Unused Section 250 deduction (due to taxable income limitation) cannot be carried back or forward. It is lost.
Interaction with Foreign Tax Credit: Section 250 deduction is taken before foreign tax credit calculation. This reduces the amount of U.S. tax available for foreign tax credit.
Example: GILTI inclusion: $1,000 Section 250 deduction (50%): $500 Net GILTI subject to tax: $500 U.S. tax (21%): $105 Foreign tax credit (80% of $150 foreign taxes): $120 (limited to $105) Net U.S. tax after credit: $0
Policy Rationale: The 50% deduction (10.5% effective rate) is designed to: - Be competitive with foreign tax rates - Encourage companies to keep IP in U.S. (FDII gets same rate) - Prevent double taxation (along with 80% foreign tax credit) - Simplify compliance (flat rate vs. complex calculations)
Individuals Not Eligible: Section 250 deduction is available ONLY to C corporations. Individuals, S corporations, partnerships, and trusts cannot claim it. Individual U.S. shareholders pay full tax on GILTI at ordinary rates.
Reference: IRC § 250(a)(1)(B) - GILTI deduction Reference: IRC § 250(a)(2) - Taxable income limitation Reference: IRC § 250(a)(3)(B) - Reduction to 37.5% after 2025 Reference: Treas. Reg. § 1.250(a)-1 - Section 250 deduction Reference: Form 8993 - Section 250 Deduction
