Section 250 GILTI Deduction - After 2025 (Reduced Rate)
For tax years beginning after December 31, 2025: - GILTI deduction rate: 37.5% (reduced from 50%) - FDII deduction rate: 21.875% (reduced from 37.5%)
Effective Tax Rate on GILTI (After 2025): - GILTI inclusion: 100% - Section 250 deduction: 37.5% - Net GILTI subject to tax: 62.5% - U.S. corporate rate: 21% - Effective rate: 21% × 62.5% = 13.125%
Rationale for Reduction: The Tax Cuts and Jobs Act (TCJA) scheduled this reduction to: - Generate additional revenue in later years - Sunset some of the TCJA benefits - Encourage current-year repatriations (higher deduction now)
Planning Opportunities: Companies may accelerate GILTI income to 2025 or earlier to benefit from the higher 50% deduction rate (10.5% effective tax).
Reference: IRC § 250(a)(3)(B) - Reduced deduction after 2025
