No Section 250 Deduction for Individuals
Section 250 deduction is available ONLY to C corporations.
Individual U.S. Shareholders: - No Section 250 deduction allowed - GILTI included in gross income at full amount - Taxed at ordinary income tax rates (up to 37% for 2025) - May claim foreign tax credit (80% of foreign taxes)
Effective Tax Rate for Individuals: Assuming top bracket (37%) and 80% foreign tax credit: - GILTI inclusion: $1,000 - U.S. tax at 37%: $370 - Foreign tax credit (80% of foreign taxes): Variable - Net U.S. tax: $370 minus foreign tax credit
Much Higher Tax Than C Corporations: Individuals face 37% rate vs. 10.5% effective rate for C corporations. This creates incentive to hold CFCs through C corporation structure.
Pass-Through Entities: S corporations, partnerships, and trusts also ineligible for Section 250. GILTI passes through to individual owners, taxed at individual rates.
Section 962 Election: Individuals may elect under IRC § 962 to be taxed as a corporation on GILTI (21% rate, eligible for Section 250 deduction and foreign tax credit). However, subsequent distributions are taxed as dividends.
Reference: IRC § 250(a)(1) - Deduction limited to corporations Reference: IRC § 962 - Individual election to be taxed as corporation Reference: Treas. Reg. § 1.962-1 - Election procedure
