Deduction Eligible Income (DEI) Calculation.
**Purpose**: - DEI is the base for calculating FDII - Represents income from non-excluded sources - Must exclude certain types of income
**Formula** (IRC § 250(b)(2)): DEI = Gross Income - Exclusions - Deductions
**Exclusions from DEI** (IRC § 250(b)(3)(A)(i)): 1. Subpart F income (IRC § 951) 2. GILTI (IRC § 951A) 3. Financial services income (IRC § 904(d)(2)(D)) 4. Dividends from CFCs 5. Domestic oil and gas income (IRC § 907(c)(1)) 6. Foreign branch income
**Example**: - Gross income: $10,000,000 - Subpart F income: $500,000 - GILTI: $300,000 - Total deductions: $6,000,000 - DEI = $10,000,000 - $800,000 - $6,000,000 = $3,200,000
Reference: IRC § 250(b)(2) Reference: IRC § 250(b)(3)(A)(i)
