// 65% DRD for ownership 20-79.9% if (result.drd_domestic_dividends_20to80 > 0) { result.drd_domestic_65pct_tentative = result.drd_domestic_dividends_20to80 * result.drd_rate_65pct; } else { result.drd_domestic_65pct_tentative = 0.0; }
// 100% DRD for ownership ≥ 80% (affiliated group) // Not subject to taxable income limitation if (result.drd_domestic_dividends_80plus > 0) { result.drd_domestic_100pct_tentative = result.drd_domestic_dividends_80plus * result.drd_rate_100pct; result.drd_domestic_100pct_allowed = result.drd_domestic_100pct_tentative; } else { result.drd_domestic_100pct_tentative = 0.0; result.drd_domestic_100pct_allowed = 0.0; }
// Store total domestic dividends result.drd_domestic_dividends_total = result.drd_domestic_dividends_lt20 + result.drd_domestic_dividends_20to80 + result.drd_domestic_dividends_80plus;
// Calculate taxable income before DRD for limitation purposes // This is total income minus deductions, before DRD and NOL result.drd_taxable_income_before_drd = result.taxable_income_before_nol;
Dividends Received Deduction - Domestic Corporations (IRC § 243).
**DRD Percentages Based on Ownership**:
1. **50% DRD** (IRC § 243(a)(1)): - Applies to dividends from corporations owned < 20% - Subject to taxable income limitation
2. **65% DRD** (IRC § 243(c)): - Applies to dividends from corporations owned ≥ 20% but < 80% - Subject to taxable income limitation
3. **100% DRD** (IRC § 243(a)(3)): - Applies to dividends from affiliated group members (≥ 80% ownership) - NOT subject to taxable income limitation - Affiliated group: 80% vote and 80% value
**Holding Period Requirement** (IRC § 246(c)): - Stock must be held > 45 days during 91-day period - For preferred stock: > 90 days during 181-day period - No DRD if holding period not met
**Example**: Corporation receives $100,000 dividends from 15% owned subsidiary: - Ownership: 15% (less than 20%) - DRD percentage: 50% - Tentative DRD: $50,000 (subject to limitation)
Reference: IRC § 243(a), IRC § 243(c) Reference: IRC § 246(c) (holding period)
