Holding Period Requirement Not Met - DRD Disallowed (IRC § 246(c)).
**Holding Period Rules**: - Common stock: Must hold > 45 days during 91-day period (beginning 45 days before ex-dividend date) - Preferred stock: Must hold > 90 days during 181-day period
**Purpose**: Prevents "dividend stripping" where taxpayers buy stock shortly before dividend, claim DRD, then sell at a loss.
**No DRD if Not Met**: Full dividend amount is taxable. No partial DRD allowed.
**Example**: - Corporation buys stock 30 days before dividend - Receives $100,000 dividend, 15% ownership - Holding period: 30 days (less than required 45 days) - DRD allowed: $0 - Taxable dividend: $100,000
Reference: IRC § 246(c)(1) Reference: IRC § 246(c)(3) (preferred stock)
