DRD Limitation Exception - Loss Position (IRC § 246(b)(2)).
**No Limitation When**: Taxable income (before DRD and NOL) is zero or negative.
**Rationale**: DRD creates or increases Net Operating Loss (NOL). NOL can be carried forward indefinitely (subject to 80% limitation). Therefore, tax benefit is preserved.
**Example**: - Operating loss: ($100,000) - Dividend income: $200,000 - Taxable income before DRD: $100,000 - 50% DRD tentative: $100,000 - Taxable income after DRD: $0
Without exception: DRD limited to $50,000 (50% × $100,000) With exception: Full $100,000 DRD allowed
Result: $0 taxable income (vs. $50,000 without exception)
**Effect on NOL**: If corporation has operating loss, full DRD increases NOL carryforward, preserving the tax benefit.
Reference: IRC § 246(b)(2) (exception) Reference: IRC § 172 (NOL carryforward)
