DRD Taxable Income Limitation Applied (IRC § 246(b)).
**Limitation Rules**:
1. **50% DRD Limited**: - Cannot exceed 50% of taxable income (before DRD and NOL) - Allowed = MIN(tentative 50% DRD, 50% × TI)
2. **65% DRD Limited**: - Cannot exceed 65% of taxable income (before DRD and NOL) - Allowed = MIN(tentative 65% DRD, 65% × TI)
3. **100% DRD NOT Limited**: - Affiliated group dividends (≥ 80% ownership) - IRC § 245A foreign dividends - Full deduction regardless of taxable income
**Example with Limitation**: - Taxable income before DRD: $100,000 - Dividends received (15% ownership): $150,000 - Tentative 50% DRD: $75,000 - Limitation (50% × $100,000): $50,000 - DRD allowed: $50,000 (LIMITED) - Taxable income after DRD: $50,000
**Example without Limitation**: - Taxable income before DRD: $200,000 - Dividends received (15% ownership): $100,000 - Tentative 50% DRD: $50,000 - Limitation (50% × $200,000): $100,000 - DRD allowed: $50,000 (not limited) - Taxable income after DRD: $150,000
**Planning Note**: Limitation only affects 50% and 65% DRD. Consider structuring to achieve 80%+ ownership for unlimited DRD.
Reference: IRC § 246(b)(1) (limitation) Reference: IRC § 243(a)(3) (100% DRD not limited)
