// When full DRD would create or increase NOL, // no limitation applies
result.drd_limitation_applies = false; result.drd_limitation_exception = true;
// Allow full tentative DRD amounts result.drd_domestic_50pct_allowed = result.drd_domestic_50pct_tentative; result.drd_domestic_65pct_allowed = result.drd_domestic_65pct_tentative;
// Calculate total DRD result.drd_total_allowed = result.drd_domestic_50pct_allowed + result.drd_domestic_65pct_allowed + result.drd_domestic_100pct_allowed + result.drd_section_245a_deduction;
// Check if DRD creates NOL double taxable_income_after_drd = result.drd_taxable_income_before_drd - result.drd_total_allowed;
// Add to audit trail if (result.audit_trail == null) { result.audit_trail = ""; } result.audit_trail = result.audit_trail + "DRD TAXABLE INCOME LIMITATION - EXCEPTION (IRC § 246(b)(2)):\n" + "Taxable income before DRD: $" + String.format("%.2f", result.drd_taxable_income_before_drd) + "\n" + "Full DRD would create NOL - no limitation applies.\n" + "Total DRD allowed: $" + String.format("%.2f", result.drd_total_allowed) + "\n" + "Taxable income after DRD: $" + String.format("%.2f", taxable_income_after_drd) + "\n" + "NOL created: $" + String.format("%.2f", Math.abs(taxable_income_after_drd)) + "\n\n";
DRD Creates NOL - Limitation Exception (IRC § 246(b)(2)).
**Exception to Limitation**: If claiming full DRD would create or increase a Net Operating Loss, the taxable income limitation does not apply.
**Rationale**: Tax benefit is preserved through NOL carryforward. NOL can offset future taxable income (subject to 80% limitation).
**Example**: - Gross income: $150,000 - Business expenses: $100,000 - Dividend income: $100,000 - Taxable income before DRD: $150,000 - Tentative 50% DRD: $50,000
Scenario A (with limitation): - Limited DRD: $50,000 (50% × $150,000) - Taxable income: $100,000 - Current tax: $21,000
Scenario B (exception applies): - Full DRD: $50,000 (no limitation) - Taxable income: $100,000 - Same result, but if DRD were larger, exception would apply
**Complex Example**: - Gross income: $80,000 - Business expenses: $100,000 - Dividend income: $100,000 - Taxable income before DRD: $80,000 - Tentative 50% DRD: $50,000 - With limitation: $40,000 (50% × $80,000) - Taxable income: $40,000
But if we allow full $50,000 DRD: - Taxable income: $30,000
Since this doesn't create NOL, limitation applies. Exception only applies when full DRD creates negative TI.
Reference: IRC § 246(b)(2) Reference: IRC § 172 (NOL rules)
