// ======================================== // Foreign Branch Income (IRC § 904(d)(1)(E)) // ========================================
// Step 1: Translate functional currency income to USD // (using average exchange rate per IRC § 987) foreign_branch.usd_gross_income = foreign_branch.fc_gross_income * foreign_branch.avg_exchange_rate;
foreign_branch.usd_deductions = foreign_branch.fc_deductions * foreign_branch.avg_exchange_rate;
foreign_branch.usd_net_income = foreign_branch.usd_gross_income - foreign_branch.usd_deductions;
// Step 2: Allocate home office expenses to branch // (interest, R&D, stewardship per Treas. Reg. § 1.861-8) double total_allocated_expenses = foreign_branch.interest_expense_allocated + foreign_branch.rd_expense_allocated + foreign_branch.stewardship_expense_allocated + foreign_branch.home_office_expense_allocated;
// Step 3: Foreign branch basket income // = Branch net income (translated) - Allocated expenses foreign_branch.ftc_branch_basket_income = foreign_branch.usd_net_income - total_allocated_expenses;
// Step 4: Translate foreign taxes paid foreign_branch.usd_foreign_taxes_paid = foreign_branch.fc_foreign_taxes_paid * foreign_branch.avg_exchange_rate;
foreign_branch.ftc_branch_basket_taxes = foreign_branch.usd_foreign_taxes_paid;
// Step 5: Update result entity for FTC calculation result.ftc_foreign_branch_income = foreign_branch.ftc_branch_basket_income; result.ftc_foreign_branch_taxes = foreign_branch.ftc_branch_basket_taxes;
// Step 6: Calculate branch E&P (in USD) foreign_branch.branch_current_ep = foreign_branch.ftc_branch_basket_income;
**Foreign Branch Income - Separate Basket (IRC § 904(d)(1)(E))**
Foreign branch income is calculated as: 1. Branch gross income (translated to USD at average rate) 2. Minus: Branch deductions (translated to USD) 3. Minus: Allocated home office expenses
**Translation Rules (IRC § 987)**: - Income/expenses: Average exchange rate for the year - Balance sheet items: Spot rate at year-end - Remittances: Spot rate at date of remittance
**Expense Allocation**: - Interest expense: Asset-based or gross income method (Treas. Reg. § 1.861-10) - R&D expense: Sales method or gross income method (Treas. Reg. § 1.861-17) - Stewardship expense: Factual relationship - General & administrative: Gross income method
**Separate Basket Requirement**: Foreign branch income CANNOT be combined with: - General basket income (active business of CFCs) - Passive basket income (dividends, interest, rents, royalties) - GILTI basket (tested income from CFCs) - Treaty basket (specific treaty income)
**Policy Rationale** (TCJA 2017): Prior to TCJA, branch income was in general basket alongside CFC income. This allowed cross-crediting of high foreign taxes on branch income against low foreign taxes on CFC income.
Separate branch basket prevents cross-crediting abuse and ensures foreign tax credit is properly limited by foreign tax rate on branch income.
**Example**: US Corp has: - UK branch income: $1,000,000 (UK tax: $250,000 = 25% rate) - Ireland CFC GILTI: $1,000,000 (Irish tax: $125,000 = 12.5% rate) - US tax (21%): $420,000 on $2,000,000
**With Separate Baskets**: - UK branch basket limitation: $210,000 (US tax on UK income) - FTC allowed: $210,000 (lesser of $250,000 paid or $210,000 limit) - Excess FTC: $40,000 (carryover) - GILTI basket limitation: $210,000 (US tax on GILTI) - FTC allowed: $100,000 (80% of $125,000 per § 960(d)) - No excess FTC from branch basket available
**Without Separate Baskets** (pre-TCJA): - Combined limitation: $420,000 - Total FTC allowed: $375,000 ($250,000 + $125,000) - No carryover needed - Effective cross-crediting of high UK tax against low Irish tax
Reference: IRC § 904(d)(1)(E) Reference: IRC § 904(d)(2)(J)(i) Reference: Treas. Reg. § 1.904-4(f) Reference: IRC § 987 (translation rules)
