// ======================================== // Section 987 Realized Gain/Loss on Remittance // ========================================
// Step 1: Calculate remittance proportion // (remittance as percentage of total QBU net assets) if (foreign_branch.net_assets_fc_beginning > 0) { foreign_branch.remittance_proportion = foreign_branch.remittance_amount_fc / foreign_branch.net_assets_fc_beginning; } else { foreign_branch.remittance_proportion = 0.0; }
// Limit proportion to 100% if (foreign_branch.remittance_proportion > 1.0) { foreign_branch.remittance_proportion = 1.0; }
// Step 2: Translate remittance to USD foreign_branch.remittance_amount_usd = foreign_branch.remittance_amount_fc * foreign_branch.spot_rate_remittance;
// Step 3: Recognize proportional share of deferred § 987 gain/loss foreign_branch.section_987_realized_gain_loss = foreign_branch.section_987_cumulative_deferred_gain_loss * foreign_branch.remittance_proportion;
// Step 4: Reduce deferred gain/loss pool foreign_branch.section_987_cumulative_deferred_gain_loss -= foreign_branch.section_987_realized_gain_loss;
// Step 5: Include realized gain/loss in taxable income // Character: Ordinary income or loss (not capital) result.other_income += foreign_branch.section_987_realized_gain_loss;
// Step 6: Adjust branch E&P foreign_branch.branch_ep_adjustment_section_987 = foreign_branch.section_987_realized_gain_loss;
**Section 987 Recognition on Remittance**
Remittance from QBU to owner triggers recognition of deferred § 987 gain/loss.
**Proportional Recognition**: Recognized amount = Cumulative deferred gain/loss × Remittance proportion
Remittance proportion = Remittance amount ÷ QBU net assets
**Example**: - Cumulative deferred § 987 gain: $100,000 - QBU net assets: €1,000,000 - Remittance: €250,000 (25% of net assets) - Recognized § 987 gain: $25,000 (25% of $100,000) - Remaining deferred gain: $75,000
**Character of Gain/Loss**: - Ordinary income or loss (not capital gain/loss) - Sourced based on location of QBU - Included in foreign branch basket for FTC purposes
**Tax Treatment**: - Gain: Increases taxable income (ordinary income) - Loss: Decreases taxable income (ordinary deduction) - No capital gain preferential rate - No Section 1231 treatment
**E&P Impact**: § 987 gain/loss adjusts branch E&P for book/tax differences.
**Policy Rationale**: Remittance represents permanent repatriation of funds. Currency gain/loss is realized when funds leave QBU.
Reference: IRC § 987(3) Reference: Treas. Reg. § 1.987-5 Reference: Treas. Reg. § 1.987-12 (recognition events)
