// ======================================== // Section 987 Full Recognition on Termination // ========================================
// Step 1: Recognize ALL deferred § 987 gain/loss foreign_branch.termination_section_987_gain_loss = foreign_branch.section_987_cumulative_deferred_gain_loss;
foreign_branch.section_987_realized_gain_loss = foreign_branch.termination_section_987_gain_loss;
// Step 2: Zero out deferred pool foreign_branch.section_987_cumulative_deferred_gain_loss = 0.0;
// Step 3: Include in taxable income result.other_income += foreign_branch.section_987_realized_gain_loss;
// Step 4: Adjust branch E&P foreign_branch.branch_ep_adjustment_section_987 = foreign_branch.section_987_realized_gain_loss;
// Step 5: Final branch E&P calculation foreign_branch.branch_accumulated_ep += foreign_branch.branch_current_ep + foreign_branch.branch_ep_adjustment_section_987;
**Section 987 Full Recognition on QBU Termination**
Termination of QBU triggers recognition of ALL deferred § 987 gain/loss.
**Termination Events**: - QBU ceases to exist - QBU incorporated (becomes separate entity) - QBU sold or transferred - QBU ceases to meet QBU definition
**Tax Treatment**: - Entire cumulative deferred § 987 gain/loss recognized - Ordinary income or loss character - Included in year of termination - Cannot be deferred further
**Example**: - Cumulative deferred § 987 gain: $500,000 (over 10 years) - QBU incorporated into foreign subsidiary - Full $500,000 gain recognized in year of incorporation - Taxable at 21% corporate rate = $105,000 US tax - May qualify for FTC if foreign tax paid
**Planning Considerations**: - Large deferred § 987 gains may discourage QBU termination - Consider gradual remittances to spread recognition over years - Incorporation of QBU accelerates gain recognition - Deferred losses may incentivize termination
**Alternative**: Tax-Free Incorporation (IRC § 351): If QBU incorporated under § 351, deferred § 987 gain/loss may be deferred further (but complex rules apply).
Reference: IRC § 987(3) Reference: Treas. Reg. § 1.987-8 (termination) Reference: Treas. Reg. § 1.987-12(b) (recognition events)
